# Editing {{ title }}

This is an exported Accessible Digital Textbook (ADT), not an ADT Studio project. You may edit its page HTML, then re-import the bundle into ADT Studio to regenerate Speech and other supported features.

## Round-trip compatibility

This bundle declares ADT Studio editing contract version `{{ editingContractVersion }}`. If the user may re-import it, the rules in this section are mandatory.

### Supported changes

- Edit visible text inside an existing element that has a `data-id`, and update the same key in `content/i18n/{{ language }}/texts.json` so the exported reader shows the edit before re-import.
- Edit layout with existing Tailwind utility classes or an element's inline `style` attribute.
- Replace or add image files under `images/`, referenced with relative paths such as `images/example.png`, and update an image's `alt` text.
- Add, remove, or reorder pages, and add or classify activities, as described below.
- Preview the book through its existing `index.html` and runtime files.

### Non-negotiable invariants

- Keep existing `data-id` values, page filenames, and section IDs exactly as they are, even when they look inconsistent. A `data-id` links the element to its translations, Speech audio, and highlighting, so keep it when you change the element's text, classes, or styles. Give new content new identities.
- A new element or `<img>` needs a new book-wide unique `data-id`, listed in its page's `editingContract.pageDataIds` in document order, with its visible text in `content/i18n/{{ language }}/texts.json`.
- Every page HTML file stays at the bundle root, with exactly one `#content` root and one canonical `section[data-section-id]` matching `content/pages.json`.
- Do not add custom stylesheet files, `<link rel="stylesheet">` tags, custom script files, or `<script src="...">` tags.
- Page media belongs in `images/`, never in `assets/`, a custom folder, or a remote URL.
- Do not edit compiled runtime files under `assets/` or `content/tailwind_output.css`.
- In `manifest.json`, change only `editingContract.pageOrder`, `pageDataIds`, `activities`, and `nonActivities`. Never change the editing contract version or the `frozen` baseline fields.
- Leave packaging to the user unless asked, and write any archive outside this folder: one left inside is flagged as an unexpected bundle entry on re-import.

If a requested change requires breaking one of these rules, tell the user that the result will no longer be re-importable into ADT Studio and ask before proceeding.

### Repairing a bundle ADT Studio rejected

When ADT Studio lists problems to fix, change only what they need: no images, elements, pages, scripts, or styles they don't require, and no rewriting to tidy up. Verify each fix the way ADT Studio checks it, not only that the attribute you added is there. Run the checklist at the end, and report anything you could not fix instead of guessing.

### Adding, removing, or reordering pages

Treat these files as one transaction. A structural edit is valid only when they agree:

1. Create or remove the root-level page HTML file.
2. Update `content/pages.json`: each entry needs a unique `section_id`, a unique root-level `href`, and its place in reading order. Sections that share a source page prefix (`pg001_sec001`, `pg001_sec002`) stay next to each other; to move one elsewhere, give it a new page ID.
3. Mirror that order in `manifest.json` under `editingContract.pageOrder`, as `{ "sectionId", "href" }`.
4. Set `editingContract.pageDataIds[href]` to every `data-id` in the page, in document order. Remove the key with the page.
5. Add the visible text of new `data-id` elements to `texts.json`. Remove text only when its content is intentionally removed.
6. Update `content/toc.json` when the navigation changes, and the activity classifications for added or removed pages.

A new page uses a new filename and section ID in the existing convention, for example `pg042_sec001.html` and `pg042_sec001`, and `data-section-type="content"` unless the whole page is an activity. Do not add it to `frozen.pageHtmlFingerprints`, which describes the original export.

### Activity classification

An activity asks the learner to provide, select, arrange, or manipulate an answer. Navigation links, language controls, media playback, accessibility controls, and ordinary content are not learning activities merely because they are interactive.

Use these exact Studio activity types:

| Type | Use when |
| --- | --- |
{% for activity in activityClassificationGuide %}| `{{ activity.type }}` | {{ activity.description }} |
{% endfor %}

For an activity made outside Studio that fits none of them, use `activity_custom_<descriptive_slug>`, for example `activity_custom_crossword`. The slug uses only lowercase letters, digits and underscores. Custom activities survive the round trip, but Studio may have no editor or generator for them.

A section is in at most one of `editingContract.activities` and `editingContract.nonActivities`, with the same `sectionId` and `href` as `editingContract.pageOrder`. When you move a section, remove it from the list it leaves, and never touch unrelated entries. In a legacy bundle without an editing contract, the HTML markers alone are enough: ADT Studio carries them into the manifest on the next export.

#### Positive classification

Mark the page's canonical section with its type, for example `<section data-section-id="pg004_sec002" data-section-type="activity_multiple_choice">`, remove `data-adt-non-activity`, and add `{ "sectionId", "href", "type" }` to `editingContract.activities`.

- Keep an existing `activity_*` type unless the learning mechanic itself changes, and keep the `data-section-id`.
- Name the activity: give a visible heading inside the `<section>` an HTML `id` attribute (for example `id="pg004_sec002-title"`) if it has none, and put that value in the section's `aria-labelledby`. `aria-labelledby`, `aria-describedby` and `<label for>` point to `id` attributes, never to a `data-id`. Don't add or change a `data-id` for this.
- Interactive controls need accessible names and keyboard support. Feedback goes in a status element with `role="status"` and `aria-live="polite"`.
- Custom behavior registers through an inline call to `window.adtRegisterCustomActivity(section, { validate, reset })`, never an external script file. ADT Studio keeps this script on export but never runs it in the editor.
- Do not disguise an activity as a content section: ADT Studio inspects these markers on re-import and asks the user to review unmarked interactive content.

#### Negative classification

Interactive content that is not a learning activity keeps a non-activity section type such as `content`, sets `data-adt-non-activity="true"` on its canonical section and, when an editing contract exists, is listed as `{ "sectionId", "href" }` in `editingContract.nonActivities`. Ordinary static pages need neither: use them only when controls, dragging, or activity-like data attributes would otherwise trigger review.

#### AI activity audit

To classify the whole book, read every entry in `content/pages.json` and its canonical section, decide from the learning mechanic rather than filenames or styling, and apply the positive or negative classification above. Leave uncertain pages unchanged and report them instead of guessing.

A user can ask: "Audit every page for learning activities using AGENTS.md, without changing the learning content."

## Canonical structure

```text
./
├── manifest.json
├── index.html
├── pg*_sec*.html                 # page HTML stays at the bundle root
├── images/                       # all page image files
├── content/
│   ├── pages.json                # reading order; preserve it
│   ├── toc.json
│   ├── tailwind_output.css       # generated; do not edit
│   └── i18n/{language}/
│       ├── texts.json
│       ├── speech_texts.json     # exact prepared read-aloud wording
│       ├── audios.json           # data-id to audio filename mapping
│       └── audio/                # generated speech files
└── assets/                       # ADT runtime; do not edit
```

The page shell keeps this relationship:

```html
<div id="content">
  <section data-section-id="pg001_sec001" data-section-type="content">
    <p data-id="pg001_gp001_tx001">Editable text</p>
    <img data-id="pg001_im001" src="images/pg001_im001.png" alt="Description">
  </section>
</div>
```

### Speech and localization files

- `texts.json` holds each language's displayed text. `speech_texts.json` holds the exact read-aloud wording, which may intentionally differ. `audios.json` maps text IDs to files in the matching `audio/` folder.
- When visible text changes, keep the IDs and regenerate Speech in ADT Studio after re-import. Do not fabricate audio or timestamps unless the user asks.

