## Before handing the bundle back

1. `content/pages.json` and `editingContract.pageOrder` list the same pages in the same order.
2. Every page exists at the bundle root, with a matching `editingContract.pageDataIds` entry, one `#content` root and its `section[data-section-id]`.
3. No `data-id` is duplicated or missing anywhere in the book, every `<img>` has one, and every `data-id` in a page is listed in that page's `pageDataIds` entry.
4. Every `activities` and `nonActivities` entry matches `pageOrder`, with no duplicate or conflicting classifications.
5. Page images resolve from `images/`, and every referenced file exists in the bundle.
6. No custom or remote stylesheets and no custom external scripts were added.
7. Every `aria-labelledby`, `aria-describedby` and `<label for>` value in an activity matches an `id` attribute inside the same activity section, on an element with visible text. Check it with an HTML parser or the DOM (`getElementById`), not text search: `id="…"` also matches inside `data-id="…"`.
8. No archive was left inside this folder.

ADT Studio runs the same checks on import and explains any incompatibility instead of guessing.
